{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:32:46.543099Z","id":"ef50a675ad3062d19bc151e2bcd835850c57383ff16f3a8e569ae4950d496924","body":{"detail":"The on-device-first listen, the fallback to the default recognizer on an error before any words, the stale done status guard (restarting) and the closing on error_no_match and error_speech_timeout follow the speech_to_text 7.5.0 sources, not observed behaviour. Widget tests use test/support/fake_voice.dart. The macOS preview (tool/launcher_preview.dart) exercises it by hand only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":178},"end":{"line":197},"content_hash":"e14b85232466ee07d11da5108c6b8c43f7702ca3e5709fc70b6d09d18e0cc14e"},"summary":"SpeechToTextVoice has no automated test and has not run on an Android device","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:01.122686Z","id":"519b4592322c8a6e193214b09f5e6056f8acca9af7d717ad3ad90e80ac9d98ed","body":{"detail":"isNetworkCut matches substrings of the messages MessagesApiBackend writes (\"Couldn't reach the Claude API\", \"The connection to the Claude API was lost\") and of the SocketException text (Failed host lookup, Connection refused/reset, Network is unreachable). AgentError has no transport kind, so a reworded backend message makes a background cut fail as \"Couldn't make it\" again; test/platform/network_pause_test.dart pins only the current wording.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"156f8c79642126f23fad88ab053f35078163c802f97197249f6a20c17b2c3520"},"suggested_fix":"Give AgentError a kind (or flag) for no-response transport failures, set it in both backends, and test isNetworkCut against it.","summary":"A background network cut is recognised by the AgentError's message text","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/background_work.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:37.268376Z","id":"20593bbe1876abbb2d21c0b3eadeb87da921800ac45f8f48c3a123224b08df08","body":{"detail":"begin ignores the bool from BackgroundWork.start, and the service stops itself in onTimeout and onTaskRemoved (BackgroundRunService.kt:108-114) without telling Dart. While any run stays in _active, every later begin only calls update, which BackgroundWorkChannel drops when BackgroundRunService.running is false. A run begun while Clax was backgrounded (start refused), or after the Android 15 dataSync time limit, therefore leaves every run that overlaps it without a foreground service, so its network is cut in the background again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"751563c93b1fb70a14fa644e5622172ddb388c1e7e1665f4dae7e034a3e23edf"},"suggested_fix":"Keep whether the service runs (from start's answer, plus a 'stopped' call from the service to Dart); begin calls start when it does not, and a return to the foreground with busy runs starts it again.","summary":"BackgroundRuns never learns that the service failed to start or stopped, so later runs go without it","tags":["review","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:37.268444Z","id":"6c13696f9f3187528b3b8e3b8ac448149d4b0625bbf36ee72b64fba852fff833","body":{"detail":"Nothing ties isNetworkCut to the errors MessagesApiBackend really throws: test/platform/network_pause_test.dart:21 builds the AgentError from a literal string, so rewording lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart:159 or :267 (the planned tool-loop backend replaces both call sites) silently turns every background cut back into 'Couldn't make it'. The bare substrings ('Connection refused', 'SocketException', …) also match text the backend copies from elsewhere, such as an HTTP error body. The change is small: add a network kind (or a transport flag) to AgentError in lib/agent/backend.dart:18-25, set it at messages_api_backend.dart:159 and :267, make isNetworkCut read only the kind, and add a test that drives MessagesApiBackend with a failing HttpClient through ResumingBackend. Also the ResumingBackend doc ('nothing was received, so nothing was applied', network_pause.dart:72-73) stops holding once the tool loop publishes during a run; the resend must then resume the loop rather than repeat it.","kind":"comment","references":"519b4592322c8a6e193214b09f5e6056f8acca9af7d717ad3ad90e80ac9d98ed","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"e81a3e9229a13e29f606ba06159018d9c0a3a11bdd90030a43fedc1a3303b902"},"summary":"Fix before this ships: carry the cut as an AgentErrorKind, not as message text","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/background_work.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:19.449305Z","id":"c82c3dce654439d8906cc19d739db07a1eca13c33d5e5ded9fe8da1a20644737","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"BackgroundRuns keeps whether the service runs: a false answer from start, or a 'stopped' call from the service (refused startForeground, onTimeout, onTaskRemoved), marks it down; the next begin starts it again, and AppRoot calls onForeground on resume, which restarts it while runs go on. A stale answer to an older start is ignored by generation. Evidence: flutter test test/platform -> +37 all passed, including 'a refused start is tried again by the next run', 'coming to the foreground restarts a refused service while runs go on', 'a service that stopped on its own is started again', 'a late refusal of an older start does not mark a newer one down', 'a stop by the service arrives on stopped'.","supersedes":"20593bbe1876abbb2d21c0b3eadeb87da921800ac45f8f48c3a123224b08df08","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:19.449773Z","id":"b483aa594bc545470c655544e022dd979324cb6493b6757c31e690b2a13269af","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"AgentErrorKind.network (lib/agent/backend.dart) is set by MessagesApiBackend when the API cannot be reached and when the connection breaks mid-answer; isNetworkCut reads only the kind. The ResumingBackend doc now says a backend that applies work during a run must resume rather than repeat it. Evidence: flutter test test/platform/network_pause_test.dart test/agent/messages_api_backend_test.dart -> all passed, including 'MessagesApiBackend reports an unreachable API as a network cut, which ResumingBackend waits out' (a real backend against a closed loopback port) and 'network failures are told by their kind, not their text'.","supersedes":"519b4592322c8a6e193214b09f5e6056f8acca9af7d717ad3ad90e80ac9d98ed","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:39.631197Z","id":"031609dec6e4411b79c46e5e4da679578c42494db03e839529232ddee0f78692","body":{"detail":"Every listen through AppServices.voice (built in lib/main.dart as DictationVoice.forSettings) is cued already, so the comment composer in lib/ui/app_screen.dart and ThreadDetail's dictation get the start and stop cues without changes. Auto-start is not automatic: app_screen.dart reads widget.settings.dictateComments (the same setting, so it agrees today), and a new surface such as ThreadDetail(autoDictate:) should be fed autoStartOf(voice) or AppSettings.dictateComments rather than a constant. Tests can pass a DictationVoice over FakeVoice with a recording VoiceCues (test/platform/voice_cues_test.dart RecordingCues).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":155},"content_hash":"fad53a229d22a87318137ff585cd765f72a5a64c2f82801b0f0320b98743a775"},"summary":"Surfaces that dictate on their own should take auto-start from autoStartOf(voice); cues need no code","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:39.631346Z","id":"96c8a30c5e4a7b91ac9b6a1a01a05239d551c6f79f71d116280a775b092d982b","body":{"detail":"Covered only by fakes (test/platform/voice_cues_test.dart). started() is fired unawaited just before inner.listen starts the recognizer, so the 120 ms TONE_PROP_BEEP (android/.../CuesChannel.kt) plays while recognition starts; many Android recognizers also beep on start. Check on the phone that the first words are not lost or misheard and that the two beeps are not confusing; if they are, await the cue before inner.listen or drop the start tone on Android.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"534633e449f88f0de69bca311e71c521b04a9f450ac069efddb9c91cd2cf3543"},"summary":"Start and stop cues have not run on a device: the start tone may overlap the recognizer's own beep or be heard by it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:55.998385Z","id":"9ca0b1548d747ebd2b3c9c7f3106215319768bceea52b4e31a857efb879fb4a8","body":{"detail":"ResumingTurns.turn sends the same TurnRequest again after a background network cut; the cut attempt threw, so MessagesApiRunner never called RunBudget.addTurn for it (lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart, after backend.turn). The API may still bill the cut attempt's input and the output it streamed before the cut, so with up to 3 resumes a turn the run's cost (RunCaps.costUsd) and output tokens can undercount by up to three attempts per turn. Accepted: the cost cap is a safety net, the history is cached so a resent turn's input is mostly cache reads, and counting it would need MessagesApiBackend to report partial usage on an AgentErrorKind.network error, which it does not. Test: test/platform/network_pause_test.dart 'a resumed turn runs no tool twice, is counted once and pauses the wall clock while held'.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":154},"end":{"line":180},"content_hash":"97ad2af28b6c6c011378bdda403b32c8a0e57cbbdefd38dbd8dfa77044fcc8b8"},"summary":"A turn attempt cut by the network is never priced: the run's cost and output caps leave out whatever the API billed for it","tags":["risk:cost","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:55.998455Z","id":"2422b32807c40dfe4faafd46b6a24cd5e96419829c004ea3fb6d7833734a7cbe","body":{"detail":"lib/app.dart wraps only the single-call AgentBackend in ResumingBackend (lines ~322 and ~505). Until the tool loop's composer (AgentLoop/FeedbackWorker on MessagesApiRunner) builds MessagesApiRunner(ResumingTurns(backend, presence, clock: ..., onPause: ..., onResume: ...)), a background network cut still fails a tool-loop run. Two things the composer must know: (1) the clock passed to ResumingTurns should be the run budget's clock, so maxHeld and the paused wall clock are measured alike; (2) onPause has no matching onResume when a hold ends by a cancel or by maxHeld (the turn throws instead), so a 'waiting for the network' notification state set in onPause must be cleared at the run's end, not only in onResume.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"1f3806ec459a92aacf8eb341c3c343d0c07acb45fd16b532cdea215654feee08"},"summary":"Nothing builds ResumingTurns yet: the composer of the tool loop must wrap its MessagesApiBackend in it, with the run's clock and the notification hooks","tags":["handoff","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:55.998487Z","id":"6f38eb184ee07e0c7df84c3d596168c0fc9347d543e5d1f7213dfea1738d5466","body":{"detail":"A held turn stops the run's wall clock (TurnHolds.pauseClock), so without a bound a run whose app stays in the background keeps the foreground service, its notification and the change's place in the queue indefinitely. Chosen: 10 minutes summed over every hold of one run (TurnHolds.held, shared by the run's turns), after which the network cut is thrown and the run fails with a Retry as before. Not taken: a bound per hold (a run could still be held for turns x 3 x the bound), or no bound (as ResumingBackend for the single call). The figure is a guess, not measured against how long people leave the app mid-change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"3f6a580e427e63e361785c6fb00dd5152cdb0146f19f1d1211927d753f63bc3b"},"summary":"The run's holds are bounded at 10 minutes in total (ResumingTurns.defaultMaxHeld), not per hold and not unbounded","tags":["revisit:after-phone-use","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:08:55.223143Z","id":"0acb9ed2947d9acaad20b60463379cc4093436804ea96d6790fda2f4744633f7","body":{"detail":"Flutter's PlatformPlugin.vibrateHapticFeedback maps HapticFeedback.mediumImpact to View.performHapticFeedback(KEYBOARD_TAP) and lightImpact to VIRTUAL_KEY. Both are the shortest key-click effects, feel alike on most phones, and are dropped entirely when the person has turned off 'Touch feedback' / haptics for touches. CuesChannel.kt silenced() skips the tone in vibrate mode, so in vibrate mode with touch feedback off a listen starts and stops with no cue at all, and with it on the start and stop cannot be told apart by feel. Distinct, clear vibration on Android needs the Vibrator in CuesChannel.kt: VibrationEffect.createPredefined(EFFECT_HEAVY_CLICK) to start and EFFECT_DOUBLE_CLICK to stop (API 29+, minSdk is 29) with the VIBRATE permission in AndroidManifest.xml, keeping HapticFeedback for macOS (which has no haptics for these anyway).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"6552a88100bca06dc117511ab6a9815e5bdb13fd2c47c7c39732de4e0335df4c"},"suggested_fix":"Add a 'vibrate' leg to the Android cues channel using predefined VibrationEffects (heavy click start, double click stop) and declare android.permission.VIBRATE; tests assert the cue name reaches the channel.","summary":"On Android the start and stop haptics are near-identical light ticks, and nothing vibrates when system touch feedback is off","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:08:55.223225Z","id":"e179493b0535f192d6146b48f7c20918706facece7328e81295eca7b7eff5a1d","body":{"detail":"The app cannot tell whether the device's SpeechRecognizer plays its own start earcon (speech_to_text 7.5.0's Android plugin neither plays nor suppresses one), so dropping our start tone would leave silent recognizers with no audible cue, which the request for clear audio cues rules out. ChannelVoiceCues._cue awaits the haptic before invoking play, so the tone request can reach the platform just after speech_to_text's startListening; TONE_PROP_BEEP lasts 40 ms, shorter than the recognizer's service bind and its own earcon, and a pure tone does not produce words. Awaiting the cue before inner.listen would only delay listening by two channel round trips. A doubled beep on recognizers that have their own earcon is the accepted cost. That holds only while the start tone stays short: a longer start tone should be awaited, plus its length, before inner.listen. The stop tone plays after the recognizer's done, so its length carries no transcription risk. Still to confirm on a phone, as this record says.","kind":"comment","references":"96c8a30c5e4a7b91ac9b6a1a01a05239d551c6f79f71d116280a775b092d982b","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"534633e449f88f0de69bca311e71c521b04a9f450ac069efddb9c91cd2cf3543"},"summary":"Recognizer interplay: keep the start tone, unawaited, and keep it short","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:11:00.017459Z","id":"be477e8001888c722de98cae044ecbe0dc32237102d9e49a936a602c32dc17e5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"CuesChannel.kt vibrates through the Vibrator: EFFECT_HEAVY_CLICK to start, EFFECT_DOUBLE_CLICK to stop, with createOneShot/createWaveform fallbacks when areAllEffectsSupported says no; AndroidManifest.xml has android.permission.VIBRATE; ChannelVoiceCues (platformHaptics, true on Android) no longer sends HapticFeedback there. flutter test test/platform/voice_cues_test.dart test/ui/new_sheet_test.dart: +25, All tests passed (new test: where the platform vibrates (Android), only the channel is called); flutter build apk --debug: exit 0.","supersedes":"0acb9ed2947d9acaad20b60463379cc4093436804ea96d6790fda2f4744633f7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:11:46.831944Z","id":"c6109f4abcf04fa61c069b5327823ea1ac1279d3dc0e7d22a66139548dee13f6","body":{"detail":"ResumingTurns holds a turn only once inner.turn throws AgentErrorKind.network, and the run's wall clock (RunBudget over SystemClock, 45 s for a change and 90 s for a new app in lib/agent/tools/budget.dart:25-33) runs until then. A turn already streaming when the app leaves the foreground with no foreground service keeping the network (a start refused in the background, the dataSync time spent, the service stopped on its own) does not fail at once if the block drops packets rather than resetting the connection: it stalls, the cached process is then frozen, and the socket error, if any, is seen only when the app thaws on return. By then the clock has counted the background time, so RunBudget.whenTimeUp fires (on thaw its overdue delay runs too) and MessagesApiRunner stops the run at its cap (messages_runner.dart:145-151, toolbox.stopAtCap) instead of resending the turn; test/platform/network_pause_test.dart 'a wall clock spent as the cut arrives stops the run at its cap' pins that order. A new request made in the background (the 'Failed host lookup ... errno = 7' case) is held as intended. Not checked on a device: whether Android resets or drops a blocked app's open TCP connections.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":154},"end":{"line":180},"content_hash":"97ad2af28b6c6c011378bdda403b32c8a0e57cbbdefd38dbd8dfa77044fcc8b8"},"suggested_fix":"Pause the run's clock while AppPresence is out of the foreground and no foreground service runs (or treat a time-up reached while the app was away during the turn as a cut and hold it), and check on a phone what an open stream sees when the app is backgrounded without the service.","summary":"A turn whose stream stalls in the background is ended by the run's wall clock, not held: only a cut that fails fast (DNS, refused or reset) is resumed","tags":["review","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:11:46.832296Z","id":"e5c11e0841f1cb49d5a8c25eafda3e18af6263e1accacdce55f7e1bce0f4917a","body":{"detail":"A foreground service lifts the APP_BACKGROUND block (comment 8ce145a5 on BackgroundRunService.kt), so a turn is held only when the service is not running: chiefly a change the FeedbackWorker starts while the app is in the background, where BackgroundWork.start is refused (lib/platform/background_work.dart:14-16), or after the service stopped on its own. There is then no service or ongoing notification to keep, only the queue place. Past 10 minutes away the cut is thrown and the person returns to a failed change with Retry rather than a run that carries on. On return after more than 10 minutes in a frozen process, the overdue clock.delay(maxHeld - held) and the resumed lifecycle event are both pending, and _hold throws only when the timer is handled first (timedOut && !presence.foreground at line 203), so the same return can resume or fail depending on that order.","kind":"concern","references":"6f38eb184ee07e0c7df84c3d596168c0fc9347d543e5d1f7213dfea1738d5466","span":{"start":{"line":184},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"ee14cb3e83630de2c93a110f0250bd513b96321c0618d7211c9e0c39e2108b5c"},"suggested_fix":"Decide between: no bound while the app stays in the background (resume on return, however long), or keep a bound but resend anyway when the app is back by the time the hold ends; either way, check presence.foreground after the lifecycle event has been delivered rather than racing the timer.","summary":"The 10-minute bound fails a held run that would resume, and its stated cost (keeping the service and notification) does not arise: a hold happens only when no foreground service keeps the network","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:11:46.832368Z","id":"464907fdfbc06ac56e3ed5906c2dc1a400671fb00e08a07801a79a58fb6f6379","body":{"detail":"_hold calls holds.pauseClock() then onPause?.call() before the try whose finally calls holds.resumeClock(). onPause is meant to drive a notification (concern 2422b328); if it throws synchronously, resumeClock never runs and the exception leaves turn() as a plain Object, which MessagesApiRunner rethrows (messages_runner.dart:145-148 catches only AgentError). RunBudget.endClock resets the pauses when the run ends, so only that run is affected.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":191},"end":{"line":192},"content_hash":"f81f308f8d568927e3775d13dea2225bdf7d80c2b4e6e6d38757711396143539"},"suggested_fix":"Call onPause inside the try (or guard it with try/catch and log), so pauseClock and resumeClock always pair.","summary":"onPause runs after pauseClock but outside the try, so a throwing onPause leaves the run's clock paused and escapes as a non-AgentError","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:11:46.832411Z","id":"9819b021ce8af67dfcd3b766c775a4cfe651ab5d6d6293adbbe3f0ff90fc2618","body":{"detail":"turn() builds a fresh TurnHolds when r.holds is null, so held restarts at zero on every turn and a run of many turns can be held for turns x maxHeld. MessagesApiRunner always passes its run's TurnHolds (messages_runner.dart:84-88), so today only other callers would see it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"ce3e5292641e390eb9194b206647d7713f77f4884d598a6bc2640cacc453000c"},"suggested_fix":"Say in the doc that the bound is per TurnHolds (per turn when none is given), or require holds.","summary":"With TurnRequest.holds null the maxHeld bound is per turn, not per run as the class doc says","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:20:55.537460Z","id":"d7dff0abb192094135604e8aff9bd6de38099548566c1b2bc0e099c040813047","body":{"detail":"Decided by the coordinator under the owner's words \"If thread dies because of connection, there's no retry\": a run cut by the background must not fail while the person is away. ResumingTurns (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart:131-227 since f1c07f346b12) now holds a cut turn until AppPresence.whenForeground or TurnRequest.cancelled, with no timer, so the race between an overdue maxHeld delay and the resumed lifecycle event is gone; when the app is back the turn is always sent again. The only bound left is maxResumes (3 resends per turn), which a turn reaches only by failing again after each return. Tests: test/platform/network_pause_test.dart 'a turn cut while backgrounded waits for the foreground with the run clock stopped, however long, then is sent again unchanged' (5 hours held) and 'a turn is sent again at most 3 times'.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","references":"e5c11e0841f1cb49d5a8c25eafda3e18af6263e1accacdce55f7e1bce0f4917a","span":{"start":{"line":184},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"c7e46bfcae2ce29c0aa7b65a7049aa50df75782723a472857125219ca6302c6d"},"summary":"Decided: no time bound on a hold; the bound is on resends (at most 3 per turn); a hold ends only by the foreground (resend) or a cancel","tags":["status:decided","decision","issuer:coordinator","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:20:55.537561Z","id":"1bff656011e86845f526aecdf2a4b942db3330176801dad6746beb064aefdf8b","body":{"detail":"Chosen (decision on e5c11e08, under the owner's 'If thread dies because of connection, there's no retry'): a hold ends when the app is back in the foreground (the turn is sent again) or the run is cancelled; ResumingTurns.maxResumes bounds how often one turn is sent again. Not taken: a total of 10 minutes held per run (ResumingTurns.defaultMaxHeld in f1c07f346b12), which failed a run that would have resumed and raced its timer against the resumed lifecycle event; a bound per hold. A hold happens only when no foreground service keeps the network (comment 8ce145a5), so there is no service or notification to keep alive; the cost of no bound is the change's place in the queue while the person is away.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"8b885df651eb181d3fe0e5d58e55329953981819d1842694739677da06ad02e9"},"summary":"A held turn waits for the app's return with no time bound; only resends are bounded (3 per turn). A total bound on held time (10 minutes per run) was dropped","supersedes":"6f38eb184ee07e0c7df84c3d596168c0fc9347d543e5d1f7213dfea1738d5466","tags":["revisit:after-phone-use","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:20:55.538369Z","id":"1cc75e552e66fe81bbcfce6d6131fa27f47d029f01dafb6072ce3f9de941f971","body":{"detail":"f1c07f346b12: MessagesApiBackend calls TurnRequest.onActivity on every server-sent event (ping included); ResumingTurns' _StallWatch (network_pause.dart:232-278) aborts a quiet attempt through its cancel signal and calls TurnHolds.pauseClock(since: last event), which RunBudget.pauseClock honours by not counting the time from then (budget.dart). The 'app left since the last event' rule covers the frozen-process case where the stall is seen only after the return. Remaining limit: if the run's own deadline is due before the stall's (less than 30 s of wall clock left at the last event), the time cap still ends the run. Evidence: flutter test test/platform/network_pause_test.dart test/agent/tools/budget_test.dart -> all passed, including 'a stream quiet for stallAfter in the background is aborted and held with the clock stopped from its last event', 'a stall seen only once the app is back (the process was frozen) still counts', 'a quiet stream in front is left alone', 'a stalled background turn is held with the wall clock taken back to its last event, then sent again', 'MessagesApiBackend reports each server-sent event as activity'.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":154},"end":{"line":180},"content_hash":"4576852f23b5c35988d002a6835b7ee63deedcf1632fa0962d29e0f64d2c261c"},"summary":"A stream with no server-sent event for 30 s while the app is in the background, or after it left since the last event, is aborted and held with the run's clock taken back to that event","supersedes":"c6109f4abcf04fa61c069b5327823ea1ac1279d3dc0e7d22a66139548dee13f6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:20:55.539064Z","id":"b8d846c37aba8b95e130c6ba2eb82e72040359212080b074753aa76d8d4d05f6","body":{"detail":"f1c07f346b12, ResumingTurns._hold (network_pause.dart:218-226). Evidence: test 'a throwing onPause still leaves the run clock running' passes (pauses 1, resumes 1); with onPause moved back before the try it fails.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":191},"end":{"line":192},"content_hash":"c2d3f6492199bfdbfa8c4e3e6585c6c3c7f38f56bad207110f09fe9ac94b0932"},"summary":"onPause now runs inside the hold's try, whose finally resumes the run's clock","supersedes":"464907fdfbc06ac56e3ed5906c2dc1a400671fb00e08a07801a79a58fb6f6379","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:20:55.539729Z","id":"364f94ea86d641e90b6a79cafd4825420d572d90504ac4b126ca54e3e212896c","body":{"detail":"f1c07f346b12 removed maxHeld and TurnHolds.held, so a null TurnRequest.holds no longer changes any bound; it only means no clock is paused. Evidence: test 'the limit is per turn: the next turn of a run may be resent again' passes.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"ff8eeeaf0d76b8d6d18b8fbdebb018a376e07254956b370c3ab29d4116ede215"},"summary":"The per-run time bound is gone (decision on e5c11e08); the remaining bound, maxResumes, is per turn and the class doc says so","supersedes":"9819b021ce8af67dfcd3b766c775a4cfe651ab5d6d6293adbbe3f0ff90fc2618","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:20:55.540372Z","id":"c1966fc77356db1ab650315686e65662fa67681b8c5d26303d28c85daa9d6c07","body":{"detail":"_StallWatch cannot tell a blocked network from a quiet model: with thinking display omitted (claude-haiku-5-5, apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart:166 sends display 'updates' only for the fallback models) a turn may send few events while the model thinks, and how often the API sends 'ping' events is not documented. Such a turn is aborted and held until the person returns, so a background run that would have finished waits for them. ResumingTurns.defaultStallAfter is 30 s for that reason (not 10 s). Measure the longest quiet stretch of real haiku turns (the backend logs could time events) and tune, or skip the stall rule while BackgroundWork reports the service running.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":142},"end":{"line":146},"content_hash":"28bd405425f63703e50e0f6f3049a789c8f9a4dfbfdb57207b02f4e48076c62f"},"summary":"A healthy stream quiet for 30 s in the background is taken for a stall and held until the app returns, even when the foreground service keeps the network","tags":["android","risk:latency","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:20:55.540427Z","id":"9c83d55ee28206945ac06b28a87d15f6c683ee291844d6f3a6b943cecdd717c4","body":{"detail":"lib/app.dart wraps only the single-call AgentBackend in ResumingBackend. Until the tool loop's composer (AgentLoop/FeedbackWorker on MessagesApiRunner) builds MessagesApiRunner(ResumingTurns(backend, presence, clock: ..., onPause: ..., onResume: ...)), a background network cut or stall still fails a tool-loop run. The composer must know: (1) the clock given to ResumingTurns should be the run budget's clock, so the stall watch and the paused wall clock are measured alike; (2) onPause has no matching onResume when a hold ends by a cancel (the turn throws instead), so a 'waiting for the network' notification state set in onPause must be cleared at the run's end, not only in onResume.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"8b885df651eb181d3fe0e5d58e55329953981819d1842694739677da06ad02e9"},"summary":"Nothing builds ResumingTurns yet: the composer of the tool loop must wrap its MessagesApiBackend in it, with the run's clock and the notification hooks","supersedes":"2422b32807c40dfe4faafd46b6a24cd5e96419829c004ea3fb6d7833734a7cbe","tags":["handoff","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.805907Z","id":"7ff1c9567596266bd5edce714911db3b43eaacf35b2ee5334cc3ca89dfe76880","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: lib/app.dart builds the tool loop's runner with toolLoopRunner(backend, presence, clock: AppServices.clock, onPause, onResume) = MessagesApiRunner(ResumingTurns(...)), and AgentLoop gets the same clock for the runs' budgets; onPause/onResume step the making screen and the BackgroundRuns notification, and each run's end ends its BackgroundRun, so a waiting step a cancel left without onResume ends with the run. The tool loop runs once an inspector is given (AppServices.inspector, Task U6). Tests in apps/clax_app/test/app_background_test.dart group 'on the tool loop': 'a turn cut by the background network block waits for the app and is sent again; the run goes on', 'a make cancelled while its turn is held ends its waiting state with the run'. flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"9c83d55ee28206945ac06b28a87d15f6c683ee291844d6f3a6b943cecdd717c4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/bundle_key.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911262Z","id":"2893fa1c456f4f7843c2c3262a0bcd7afdfd4f8149d56d6eeed3fd7cd3782cec","body":{"detail":"The regex admits any 43 characters of the alphabet, but Dart's base64Url.decode rejects a final character with non-zero low bits (checked: 'AAA…AB' throws 'Invalid encoding before padding'). The doc comment promises null for anything not a 32-byte base64url key.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":169},"content_hash":"d80b8ddc37a8ff7c46d5d1c42804481347a201cd63180e539458ea91585387bb"},"suggested_fix":"Catch FormatException and return null, or tighten the last character to [AEIMQUYcgkosw048].","summary":"keyFingerprint throws on a 43-character key with non-zero trailing bits instead of returning null","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/bundle_key.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:52.171742Z","id":"108a474d06d2abc562c9c38c92189a0cc39c916465109aaaba45dc69da1cf99b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"keyFingerprint catches the decoder's FormatException and returns null. Evidence: flutter test test/bundle/trust_test.dart test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart test/platform/bundle_key_test.dart -> +36, All tests passed, including keyFingerprint('A'*42+'B') == null in the fingerprint test.","supersedes":"2893fa1c456f4f7843c2c3262a0bcd7afdfd4f8149d56d6eeed3fd7cd3782cec","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:05:45.974552Z","id":"0e3a5b1455d20b9bcd1da3079519eae28e7f10121903401e7be290a44be0d4e3","body":{"detail":"Waits for the connection are not counted against maxResumes (lines 257-262). The probe (canConnect, apps/clax_app/lib/platform/connection.dart:102:118) is a TCP connect to api.anthropic.com:443, so a captive portal or a TLS-breaking proxy passes it while every request fails with AgentErrorKind.network: the run shows 'Waiting for connection' and resends at the probe's interval (2 s doubling to 30 s) until cancelled. Nothing is billed for a request that never reached the API, but the change never fails either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"fa062a9d595ff357245e13b4feeb010b2449c98a8d47d658eb8a32108ca0437b"},"suggested_fix":"Probe with an HTTPS request to the API (any HTTP status counts as reachable), or count waits whose probe answered at once and fail after a bound.","summary":"A turn whose resends keep failing as network cuts while the connection probe answers waits and resends without bound","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:05:45.974646Z","id":"427df2cbbc86604f56a34e863b90861d6498795d538f5038d24bda1d67ab58f2","body":{"detail":"A transient probe failure (5 s connect timeout on a slow network) while the model thinks quietly aborts the attempt and resends the same turn once the probe answers. What the aborted attempt was billed is not priced (waiver 9ca0b154), so a run can cost more than its counted cost. The 30 s threshold is defaultStallAfter, tuned for the background (c1966fc7).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":358},"end":{"line":369},"content_hash":"565db1889a3f01f758fa623ab43b2feaaa9458d1e8d7e23c73270828109f3317"},"summary":"In front, a stream quiet for 30 s is probed; a probe that fails then aborts a healthy but slow turn and sends it again","tags":["revisit:phone use shows resends of healthy turns in front","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/connection.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:05:45.974835Z","id":"e2bb80a71915c4f8ce7eb38dfa18e5a4c08b66c4f5d0e9865589c91d6b14162e","body":{"detail":"ResumingBackend and ResumingTurns wait only on AgentErrorKind.network, which MessagesApiBackend sets. ClaudeCliBackend never does, so with the claude -p backend a make or change without a connection still fails as before. Waiting runs also hold their slots: up to three changes (FeedbackWorker.maxConcurrent) and three makes (MakeService.maxRunning) wait at once and later ones queue behind them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"4bd61165e30a54c4367cdd756659df558f9dffda28c64141836ad4f4cdc97059"},"summary":"Only the Messages API backends wait for the connection: claude -p (macOS) reports an unreachable API as an ordinary failure","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:09:09.471381Z","id":"a58b6ae31955d92ed18aee0a33d251eab58ac57dc57b8bda38c5929d362ba1bd","body":{"detail":"Failure: in front, on a connection where TCP to api.anthropic.com:443 opens but streams drop part way (weak cell, a train, a flaky Wi-Fi), MessagesApiBackend reports each break as AgentErrorKind.network (messages_api_backend.dart:424). ResumingTurns calls connection.lost() and waits; maxResumes no longer applies (lines 247-262). lost() starts a fresh _probeLoop (connection.dart:73-90) whose wait is a local reset to firstProbe, so the probe answers after 2 s and the same turn is sent again, and again, until the person cancels. Each attempt reached the API and is billed (its input, mostly cache reads, plus the output streamed before the break), but a failed attempt never reaches RunBudget.addTurn, so RunCaps.costUsd never stops the run. Waiver 9ca0b154 accepted this undercount on the premise of 'up to three attempts per turn'; this path removes that bound. Concern 0e3a5b14 covers the captive-portal case (no API billing) and says the cadence doubles to 30 s; it does not, since each lost() restarts the backoff.","kind":"blocker","references":"0e3a5b1455d20b9bcd1da3079519eae28e7f10121903401e7be290a44be0d4e3","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"fa062a9d595ff357245e13b4feeb010b2449c98a8d47d658eb8a32108ca0437b"},"suggested_fix":"Count connection waits whose probe answered at its first try (the connection was not really lost) against maxResumes, or keep the backoff across lost() calls within one turn; past the bound, throw the network error so the run fails as before.","summary":"A turn whose stream keeps breaking mid-answer in front is resent every ~2 s without bound, and none of the billed attempts is counted","tags":["risk:cost","offline","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/connection.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:09:09.471421Z","id":"87b10768bb0d4ad3f887e14f89a2026240d3734d544fd927d358d12cf8ab89d6","body":{"detail":"Once lost() or a failed check() set ApiConnection offline, _probeLoop probes every 30 s (after the backoff) until a probe answers, whether or not any run still waits on whenOnline: a change or make cancelled while offline, or the device simply staying offline, keeps a TCP connect attempt (and DNS lookup) every 30 s for as long as the process runs, including in the background with the foreground service gone. Each probe wakes the radio. Not checked on a device.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"87692998a9d50945182c9b5f48a66d2d9acb564d44190757ed1a9edf15b8a8c3"},"suggested_fix":"Stop probing when no whenOnline future is pending (track waiters) and when AppPresence is out of the foreground; didChangeAppLifecycleState already calls check() on resume.","summary":"The probe loop keeps running while nothing waits for the connection, in the background too","tags":["battery","offline","review","unverified-on-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:24:13.271142Z","id":"bdb9eb801112acabca4a66a0e3d4754f9a4b6ee539aa89622fda72c241e566a0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"A turn cut in front is sent again at most maxOfflineResends (5) times, then waits for ApiConnection.nudge (back in front, or Try now); each cut attempt that reached the API is counted as a turn of the last turn's input (TurnHolds.onCutAttempt, MessagesApiRunner); lost() soon after a return doubles the interval instead of restarting it. Evidence: test/platform/network_pause_test.dart 'a stream that keeps breaking mid-answer while the probe passes is sent again at most maxOfflineResends times, then waits for a nudge' and the stalled-turn test now counting 2 turns; test/platform/connection_test.dart 'a loss soon after the API came back keeps backing off'; all pass.","supersedes":"a58b6ae31955d92ed18aee0a33d251eab58ac57dc57b8bda38c5929d362ba1bd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:24:13.276728Z","id":"5ad95009507c6c863e035359433f405df134096685ac08a4f471601cf9c97fa9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Bounded: a network that passes the probe but fails every request is sent again at most 5 times per turn, then waits for the app's return to the front or Try now (same evidence as the resolve of a58b6ae3).","supersedes":"0e3a5b1455d20b9bcd1da3079519eae28e7f10121903401e7be290a44be0d4e3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/connection.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:24:13.282102Z","id":"1955c03ded5aabb374ad6f709929f8fd3ae89bf4ce87a4463ff96085c1442196","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The probe loop runs only while a waitOnline is pending and ApiConnection.foreground is true (the app sets it on each lifecycle change and nudges on resume, f1c07f346b12). Evidence: test/platform/connection_test.dart 'nothing is probed while no run waits…' and 'in the background it stops probing; back in front it checks at once…' pass.","supersedes":"87b10768bb0d4ad3f887e14f89a2026240d3734d544fd927d358d12cf8ab89d6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:02:34.131833Z","id":"cd9ed3316acea71a25ecdac41fff261bf2915b09192dc46967c4913cab7a2de7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9ca0b1548d747ebd2b3c9c7f3106215319768bceea52b4e31a857efb879fb4a8","summary":"Superseded: since f1c07f346b12 a cut attempt that reached the API is priced (an estimate of its input and streamed output, TurnHolds.onCutAttempt and _Run._cutAttempt in apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart) and counted as a turn, and a cap it reaches ends the run. A cut that never reached the API (no stream event) is still not priced, as nothing was billed.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:02:53.560156Z","id":"6e3be3d63528fc393b8427dd55cf185e961f6e5817b8bcf31bb0da5a8cd66d74","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Superseded by f1c07f346b12: cut attempts that reached the API are now priced and counted (reply cd9ed331); evidence in the resolve of f8183d04 (test each cut attempt that reached the API is priced... passes).","supersedes":"9ca0b1548d747ebd2b3c9c7f3106215319768bceea52b4e31a857efb879fb4a8","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:02.421181Z","id":"118201db1152a64ee3269b868760021c6ecd9767c09c66b6d6b2f472602173bf","body":{"detail":"As a network cut does (record 9ca0b154, superseded by the pricing of cut attempts): an attempt the pause aborted after its stream sent an event is told to TurnHolds.onCutAttempt and priced as a turn, so each pause in one turn adds a turn and its estimated cost to the run's budget. Many pauses in one turn can therefore reach the run's turn or cost cap (RunCaps in apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/budget.dart) even though maxResumes does not count them. Accepted: iOS gives about 30 s of background time per leave, and the alternative (letting the request finish in the background) is the BGContinuedProcessingTask path the owner declined.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":350},"end":{"line":354},"content_hash":"1d9cdb15b0936f3b59a51308fddb925736dbad83300225289f143cc92f71c7a8"},"summary":"A pause aborts a turn attempt that may already have been billed; a pause near the end of a long answer costs that answer again","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:00:31.628912Z","id":"17218d69c670b4a52b7aa0c01bf912e022ad05b77292b8e3d5108146ddf53cf1","body":{"detail":"No channel serves dev.empathic.clax/cues on iOS (ios/Runner has no cues handler), so with platformHaptics true an iOS dictation cue would neither vibrate nor sound. platformHaptics stays Platform.isAndroid, so iOS plays HapticFeedback.mediumImpact and lightImpact (UIKit's impact generator), as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md's platform table says; test/platform/voice_cues_test.dart pins it with the isAndroid parameter.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":42},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"14cbc17694b4975ddbbe09d197e4ced691456766541305f4dd35e8507fbd1459"},"summary":"platformHaptics true on iOS (the platform's play vibrating) was not taken","tags":["ios","revisit:an iOS cues channel that plays a tone and a haptic of its own","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:21:34.315419Z","id":"8f491fad33fcd17b458433f1e62152ed9f188a3373678c32e0f88e1b13b41ab8","body":{"detail":"VoiceError's message is the plugin's exception text ('$e', line 197) or speech_to_text's errorMsg code (error_no_match, error_speech_timeout, error_network; line 222). apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:1699 and apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart:522 log it and show the plain line, so the person cannot tell no speech heard from a network failure.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":197},"end":{"line":222},"content_hash":"9d8dcab1258022434329d20c881559d9259434afadae968f1afcbafd91ee5353"},"suggested_fix":"Map the speech_to_text codes to plain sentences in VoiceError (\"Didn’t hear anything.\", \"Dictation needs the internet.\") and show those.","summary":"A dictation error reads only \"Dictation stopped. Try again.\": VoiceError carries the plugin's raw text, so the screens no longer show it","tags":["copy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:02:15.621804Z","id":"9ea81cdc0c1c3aa1e94089561814fa512664e3313bfd7c371b7e30827bc3c6e7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: VoiceError keeps the plugin's code for the log and answers a plain message through voiceErrorLine (nothing heard, microphone access, internet, busy, or stopped), which the app screen and thread detail show; no match or a speech timeout before any words now reads as nothing heard. Evidence: `bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:platform_voice_error_test` at f1c07f346b12 -> PASSED ('each common recognizer code reads as its own plain line').","supersedes":"8f491fad33fcd17b458433f1e62152ed9f188a3373678c32e0f88e1b13b41ab8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/settings_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:53:57.725493Z","id":"cb0d10822e3251f04e10344328c2ff7c0059482af275a512a67ca292ef0a9a8f","body":{"detail":"Left in place: about 70 widget tests in 20 files build SettingsStore over a real file, and an asynchronous read or write never completes in their fake time, so moving it needs those tests on tester.runAsync or a store fake. The file is a few hundred bytes; the fsync on save (an Android flash fsync can take milliseconds) happens on a person's setting change, not while a page loads. The same shape (sync IO inside async calls, for the same tests) is in lib/platform/device/device_grants.dart:183-241, lib/platform/device/reminders.dart:94-115, lib/agent/stops.dart:48-69, lib/agent/unfinished.dart:226-281, lib/ui/read_consent_dialog.dart:59-106 and lib/bundle/doc_snapshot.dart:163-347 (a live migration's journal, synced per write).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":222},"end":{"line":249},"content_hash":"2abd716e92920a5a02479c5e1a89e9528a4ecdeacad8891531565bc8cf317efc"},"suggested_fix":"Give the stores one serialized writer on dart:io's async calls (or a background isolate), and move their widget tests to tester.runAsync or in-memory stores.","summary":"SettingsStore still reads and writes settings.json synchronously on the UI isolate, and each save fsyncs (flush: true) before its rename","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/bundle_intake.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:20:46.727572Z","id":"725a5fcba8aa34411806189105cf001ab5c42e5cf5c3f0c035d78b4fe9395a06","body":{"detail":"BundleIntakeEvent.of returns null for a {url} that artifactOf does not accept, so ChannelBundleIntake never emits it and lib/app.dart cannot tell the person. Inputs: clax://get?url=… (with an authority), clax:get?url=http://…, clax:get?url=https://host/a/<id>/get, a clax.dev link with a bad ID. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-21-app-push-pull.md Task 12 asks for the refusal \"That link isn't a Clax app.\".","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"91eae4541232f2daff3bc698b9546b472230c1c83befc62bedfb78e8b97f28f3"},"suggested_fix":"Emit BundleIntakeEvent.refused('not_a_link') for a {url} that does not parse and show it through BundleNoticeSheet.refused, or decide that silence is right for links.","summary":"A link artifactOf refuses is dropped without a word: following a malformed clax: link opens Clax and shows nothing","tags":["status:needs-decision","links","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/bundle_intake.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:26:34.220404Z","id":"16688be948585042de4f3c9529e7a57da5861e28f023beb4163abf18eb739185","body":{"detail":"artifactOf checks only inner.host.isEmpty. Dart's Uri keeps percent escapes in a reg-name host. Run through the code at lines 59-98: clax:get?url=https%3A%2F%2Fclax.dev%252F.evil.example%2Fa%2F7q3k9mzx2b4t returns https://clax.dev%2F.evil.example/a/7q3k9mzx2b4t (host 'clax.dev%2F.evil.example'), and a Cyrillic look-alike clax:get?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcl%D0%B0x.dev%2Fa%2F7q3k9mzx2b4t returns host 'cl%D0%B0x.dev'. Neither host resolves, so a fetch fails, but a provenance line or error that prints the host starts with 'clax.dev'. Loopback and LAN hosts also pass (https://127.0.0.1/a/<id>, https://[::1]:7480/a/<id>, https://localhost/a/<id>), so any web page can make the app send an HTTPS GET to a local address when the person follows a link; spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md §5.5 has the link fetch the bundle before the install sheet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":94},"content_hash":"5d8bedf181f4f2c29910337670683ee0880a6e9c7a09d58a9892514710a2a641"},"suggested_fix":"Accept only an LDH host (letters, digits, '-', '.', so punycode passes and '%' does not) or an IP literal the owner chooses to allow; whoever writes the pull shows the whole host in the provenance line.","summary":"A clax:get link's inner host passes with percent-encoded bytes, so artifactOf returns hosts that are no DNS name, one of which reads as clax.dev","tags":["links","security","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/bundle_intake.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:26:34.221056Z","id":"263c0a29de6a72da4774cbc01f0e459551057725a8fd077d741740fecb17bad0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"725a5fcba8aa34411806189105cf001ab5c42e5cf5c3f0c035d78b4fe9395a06","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"91eae4541232f2daff3bc698b9546b472230c1c83befc62bedfb78e8b97f28f3"},"summary":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-21-app-push-pull.md:531 already fixes the behaviour (\"Anything else is refused with 'That link isn't a Clax app.'\"), so this is a gap rather than an open choice: BundleIntakeEvent.of could return BundleIntakeEvent.refused('not_a_link') for a {url} artifactOf refuses, with 'not_a_link' => \"That link isn’t a Clax app.\" added to apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart:33-39 (an unknown code there reads 'This file is damaged or was changed after it was signed.'), and FakeBundleIntake.openLink doing the same. Only links the native side already narrowed reach Dart (clax: on all three, https clax.dev from the Android filter and iOS universal links), so each refusal is a link the person followed toward Clax.","tags":["links","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/bundle_intake.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:44:54.195656Z","id":"980d9a109404059fe79754d06153ed6307113a3be478bbc78019ae7056d47de9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b93c9676a","summary":"BundleIntakeEvent.of now returns BundleIntakeEvent.refused('not_a_link') for a {url} artifactOf refuses (ChannelBundleIntake and FakeBundleIntake.openLink), and lib/bundle/installer.dart maps not_a_link to \"That link isn’t a Clax app.\", as docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-21-app-push-pull.md Task 12 specifies. test/platform/bundle_intake_test.dart 'a refused link says so', intake_refuses_other_urls, 'the channel delivers accepted links and refuses the rest' and 'FakeBundleIntake refuses what the platform intake refuses' pass under just test-affected (77 tests pass); with the refusal reverted to null and the copy line removed, all four fail.","supersedes":"725a5fcba8aa34411806189105cf001ab5c42e5cf5c3f0c035d78b4fe9395a06","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/bundle_intake.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:44:54.487155Z","id":"1aea4b4b525679c09238ec3ce759d116cd13f5608e7bd283e3a1561a7df83af2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"16688be948585042de4f3c9529e7a57da5861e28f023beb4163abf18eb739185","summary":"Loopback and LAN hosts are left accepted on purpose: clax:get?url=https://127.0.0.1/a/<id>, https://localhost/a/<id>, https://192.168.1.20/a/<id> and https://[::1]:7480/a/<id> still pass artifactOf (intake_parses_clax_get_and_https_get asserts it), so a web page can still make the app fetch from a local address over HTTPS. Whether to refuse them is the owner's call.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/bundle_intake.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:44:54.488090Z","id":"3c5178e20dccee1f7b3367758fb0e89cb56a79051fbe271b9671feefbcc79ed2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b93c9676a","summary":"artifactOf now requires the inner host to match ^(?:[a-z0-9.-]+|[0-9a-f:.]*:[0-9a-f:.]*)$ (LDH, punycode included, or an IPv6 address). intake_refuses_other_urls covers https://clax.dev%2F.evil.example, clax.dev%252F.evil.example, cl%D0%B0x.dev, a raw Cyrillic а, a fullwidth ｃ and an IPv6 zone ID, and passes; with the check put back to inner.host.isEmpty it fails on clax:get?url=https%3A%2F%2Fclax.dev%252F.evil.example%2Fa%2F7q3k9mzx2b4t (Actual: https://clax.dev%2F.evil.example/a/7q3k9mzx2b4t).","supersedes":"16688be948585042de4f3c9529e7a57da5861e28f023beb4163abf18eb739185","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/connection.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:03.948097Z","id":"2f1eaea5f851581fb60fa1ad5cdc3ce1e0c2cd4c784b659eb78fcb833d0cbb25","body":{"detail":"ResumingBackend and ResumingTurns wait only on AgentErrorKind.network, which MessagesApiBackend sets. ClaudeCliBackend never does, so with the claude -p backend a make or change without a connection still fails as before. Waiting runs also hold their slots: up to three changes (FeedbackWorker.maxConcurrent) and three makes (MakeService.maxRunning) wait at once and later ones queue behind them.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":28},"content_hash":"4bd61165e30a54c4367cdd756659df558f9dffda28c64141836ad4f4cdc97059"},"summary":"Only the Messages API backends wait for the connection: claude -p (macOS) reports an unreachable API as an ordinary failure","supersedes":"e2bb80a71915c4f8ce7eb38dfa18e5a4c08b66c4f5d0e9865589c91d6b14162e","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:04.136510Z","id":"f7ee48d9466ec77f794dcf8bf99200d937e4a1f470f493290121b21e96a87002","body":{"detail":"A transient probe failure (5 s connect timeout on a slow network) while the model thinks quietly aborts the attempt and resends the same turn once the probe answers. What the aborted attempt was billed is not priced (waiver 9ca0b154), so a run can cost more than its counted cost. The 30 s threshold is defaultStallAfter, tuned for the background (c1966fc7).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":498},"end":{"line":509},"content_hash":"565db1889a3f01f758fa623ab43b2feaaa9458d1e8d7e23c73270828109f3317"},"summary":"In front, a stream quiet for 30 s is probed; a probe that fails then aborts a healthy but slow turn and sends it again","supersedes":"427df2cbbc86604f56a34e863b90861d6498795d538f5038d24bda1d67ab58f2","tags":["revisit:phone use shows resends of healthy turns in front","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/settings_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:04.227277Z","id":"79f940fa04657026ca65c94d8e88ea276f14a9650971a1701bf9f438b2eb348d","body":{"detail":"Left in place: about 70 widget tests in 20 files build SettingsStore over a real file, and an asynchronous read or write never completes in their fake time, so moving it needs those tests on tester.runAsync or a store fake. The file is a few hundred bytes; the fsync on save (an Android flash fsync can take milliseconds) happens on a person's setting change, not while a page loads. The same shape (sync IO inside async calls, for the same tests) is in lib/platform/device/device_grants.dart:183-241, lib/platform/device/reminders.dart:94-115, lib/agent/stops.dart:48-69, lib/agent/unfinished.dart:226-281, lib/ui/read_consent_dialog.dart:59-106 and lib/bundle/doc_snapshot.dart:163-347 (a live migration's journal, synced per write).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":260},"end":{"line":287},"content_hash":"2abd716e92920a5a02479c5e1a89e9528a4ecdeacad8891531565bc8cf317efc"},"suggested_fix":"Give the stores one serialized writer on dart:io's async calls (or a background isolate), and move their widget tests to tester.runAsync or in-memory stores.","summary":"SettingsStore still reads and writes settings.json synchronously on the UI isolate, and each save fsyncs (flush: true) before its rename","supersedes":"cb0d10822e3251f04e10344328c2ff7c0059482af275a512a67ca292ef0a9a8f","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:04.316580Z","id":"1f2f8c91373a9012ea620ac3bc9ae44396f06fafb01c533de0f8a4e101d5df10","body":{"detail":"Covered only by fakes (test/platform/voice_cues_test.dart). started() is fired unawaited just before inner.listen starts the recognizer, so the 120 ms TONE_PROP_BEEP (android/.../CuesChannel.kt) plays while recognition starts; many Android recognizers also beep on start. Check on the phone that the first words are not lost or misheard and that the two beeps are not confusing; if they are, await the cue before inner.listen or drop the start tone on Android.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"534633e449f88f0de69bca311e71c521b04a9f450ac069efddb9c91cd2cf3543"},"summary":"Start and stop cues have not run on a device: the start tone may overlap the recognizer's own beep or be heard by it","supersedes":"96c8a30c5e4a7b91ac9b6a1a01a05239d551c6f79f71d116280a775b092d982b","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:04.407249Z","id":"14342420db983f6ea108028be30eff694b41257bf70a2b0f17e09288e19fd26c","body":{"detail":"Every listen through AppServices.voice (built in lib/main.dart as DictationVoice.forSettings) is cued already, so the comment composer in lib/ui/app_screen.dart and ThreadDetail's dictation get the start and stop cues without changes. Auto-start is not automatic: app_screen.dart reads widget.settings.dictateComments (the same setting, so it agrees today), and a new surface such as ThreadDetail(autoDictate:) should be fed autoStartOf(voice) or AppSettings.dictateComments rather than a constant. Tests can pass a DictationVoice over FakeVoice with a recording VoiceCues (test/platform/voice_cues_test.dart RecordingCues).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"fad53a229d22a87318137ff585cd765f72a5a64c2f82801b0f0320b98743a775"},"summary":"Surfaces that dictate on their own should take auto-start from autoStartOf(voice); cues need no code","supersedes":"031609dec6e4411b79c46e5e4da679578c42494db03e839529232ddee0f78692","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:45.049401Z","id":"a3f9916ddfcf7bc368ce5d95db0b5108f56aef4244682dbf8905ebcc50f6a7b7","body":{"detail":"Chosen (decision on e5c11e08, under the owner's 'If thread dies because of connection, there's no retry'): a hold ends when the app is back in the foreground (the turn is sent again) or the run is cancelled; ResumingTurns.maxResumes bounds how often one turn is sent again. Not taken: a total of 10 minutes held per run (ResumingTurns.defaultMaxHeld in f1c07f346b12), which failed a run that would have resumed and raced its timer against the resumed lifecycle event; a bound per hold. A hold happens only when no foreground service keeps the network (comment 8ce145a5), so there is no service or notification to keep alive; the cost of no bound is the change's place in the queue while the person is away.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":272},"end":{"line":311},"content_hash":"cc57492ea855b598aa698b7d53a2514323fae219d03a7ecaea0721a0f6ec62b8"},"summary":"A held turn waits for the app's return with no time bound; only resends are bounded (3 per turn). A total bound on held time (10 minutes per run) was dropped","supersedes":"1bff656011e86845f526aecdf2a4b942db3330176801dad6746beb064aefdf8b","tags":["revisit:after-phone-use","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:45.147220Z","id":"5ff757178149406a14271faa0864f6bfbedcfb3e22fa058b4129905addee831f","body":{"detail":"The on-device-first listen, the fallback to the default recognizer on an error before any words, the stale done status guard (restarting) and the closing on error_no_match and error_speech_timeout follow the speech_to_text 7.5.0 sources, not observed behaviour. Widget tests use test/support/fake_voice.dart. The macOS preview (tool/launcher_preview.dart) exercises it by hand only.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":260},"content_hash":"acdc3ea4730e93fe668dd9c13e1c81f1e22690180cee1c7bb3b971e1e62fa027"},"summary":"SpeechToTextVoice has no automated test and has not run on an Android device","supersedes":"ef50a675ad3062d19bc151e2bcd835850c57383ff16f3a8e569ae4950d496924","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:36:02.084117Z","id":"a3c7778e5e6276f295061cdd56866eb84402e7e93428fe2a780dd40f487c9300","body":{"detail":"Decided by the coordinator under the owner's words \"If thread dies because of connection, there's no retry\": a run cut by the background must not fail while the person is away. ResumingTurns (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart:131-227 since f1c07f346b12) now holds a cut turn until AppPresence.whenForeground or TurnRequest.cancelled, with no timer, so the race between an overdue maxHeld delay and the resumed lifecycle event is gone; when the app is back the turn is always sent again. The only bound left is maxResumes (3 resends per turn), which a turn reaches only by failing again after each return. Tests: test/platform/network_pause_test.dart 'a turn cut while backgrounded waits for the foreground with the run clock stopped, however long, then is sent again unchanged' (5 hours held) and 'a turn is sent again at most 3 times'.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","references":"e5c11e0841f1cb49d5a8c25eafda3e18af6263e1accacdce55f7e1bce0f4917a","span":{"start":{"line":359},"end":{"line":395},"content_hash":"0366e9d4bad63e56cabeb316324885712b9b6b35896db12c890332d4269c2904"},"summary":"Decided: no time bound on a hold; the bound is on resends (at most 3 per turn); a hold ends only by the foreground (resend) or a cancel","supersedes":"d7dff0abb192094135604e8aff9bd6de38099548566c1b2bc0e099c040813047","tags":["status:decided","decision","issuer:coordinator","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:36:02.195675Z","id":"796244f57264ee832b92f6d045499c59d7a4f4d7d7f67453b9f78827fd14e5d3","body":{"detail":"The app cannot tell whether the device's SpeechRecognizer plays its own start earcon (speech_to_text 7.5.0's Android plugin neither plays nor suppresses one), so dropping our start tone would leave silent recognizers with no audible cue, which the request for clear audio cues rules out. ChannelVoiceCues._cue awaits the haptic before invoking play, so the tone request can reach the platform just after speech_to_text's startListening; TONE_PROP_BEEP lasts 40 ms, shorter than the recognizer's service bind and its own earcon, and a pure tone does not produce words. Awaiting the cue before inner.listen would only delay listening by two channel round trips. A doubled beep on recognizers that have their own earcon is the accepted cost. That holds only while the start tone stays short: a longer start tone should be awaited, plus its length, before inner.listen. The stop tone plays after the recognizer's done, so its length carries no transcription risk. Still to confirm on a phone, as this record says.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"comment","references":"1f2f8c91373a9012ea620ac3bc9ae44396f06fafb01c533de0f8a4e101d5df10","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"534633e449f88f0de69bca311e71c521b04a9f450ac069efddb9c91cd2cf3543"},"summary":"Recognizer interplay: keep the start tone, unawaited, and keep it short","supersedes":"e179493b0535f192d6146b48f7c20918706facece7328e81295eca7b7eff5a1d","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
